ANN stands for Artificial Neural Network
    An Artificial Neural Network (ANN) is a machine learning model inspired by the structure of 
    biological neurons, consisting of interconnected layers of neurons that learn patterns from data by 
    adjusting weights and biases through forward propagation and backpropagation.

Artificial Neural Network is inspired from Biological neurons. and it consists of three layers:
    1) Input layer.
    2) Hidden layer
    3) Output layer

Input layer : 
    Receives the input features.
    Number of feature columns = Number of input features

Hidden layer:
    Processes the inputs
    learns patterns and reresentations

    An ANN can have one or many hidden layers.
    Hidden layers number is hyperparameter.
Output layer:
    predicts the output

    Number of neurons on output layer depends on the problem we are solving.
    like regression or classfication.

    for regression - only one neuron on output
    for classification - binary types(0/1 or yes/no)- one neuron
                        - multi classification - two or more neurons

information in each input passes to all hidden neurons and all hidden neuron
outputs are connected to output layers. This connection is knowns as dense connection.

Neuron : 
    Neuron can be divided into two parts
    one part can perform Math operation, another part can perform activation.

    this structure can be in all neurons except input neurons.

Weights : 
    Every connection can be carrying the weightage. Meanwhile passing information from 
    input to hidden state, it also carries the importance of the input value through the 
    connection  is known as weights.

    weights are assigned randomly.

Activations:
    Activations are used to extract the non linear relationships (each neuron extracts the complete inform
    and sends to another neuron that is both linear and non linear relationships)

    some of the important activations are :
        -ReLU
        -TanH
        -Sigmoid
        -Softmax

    activations are used in hidden and output layers

    Hidden - ReLU, Tanh

    output - Sigmoid, Softmax

ReLU(Rectified Linear Unit)

relu performs on neuron where the input is travelled from math operation the output 
becomes 0 if x is negative 
keeps as it is if x is positive 

for regression , no activation is used in output layer
for classification, sigmoid and softmax functions are used.

the input is successfully passed through hidden layers and produced at output layer
this process is known as forward propagation.

so we use backward propagation to reduce the errors.

Backward propagation:
    is performed to reduce errors by updating weights - using derivatives

    d/d(w) (error) if weight decrease , we observe that error is reducing or not.

it does several iterations both forward and backward until the error minimizes close to 
the zero.

There is a problem while updating weights that is vanishing gradient problem ,
if we keep updating the weights by minimizing , some weights become zero,
then the neuron stops passing information to other neurons

if the weights are increasing gradually in multiple iterations , particular neuron weight becomes
too large then the whole prediction depends on that feature 
this is known as exploiding gradient.

to reduce these types of problems we use batch normalisation. that is normalisation means we scale
the values in same range like -1 to 1. and batch normalisation we apply on weights instead of features
that helps in preventing the both vanishing and exploidig gradient problems.